1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,620
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,620 --> 00:00:04,980
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:06,040
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,630 --> 00:00:07,820
I've worked in a warehouse

5
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:09,210
for thirty years.

6
00:00:09,330 --> 00:00:11,010
On my feet on concrete,

7
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:12,340
lifting boxes

8
00:00:12,340 --> 00:00:14,290
and pulling pallets all
day.

9
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:15,320
I had my right knee

10
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:16,880
replaced two years ago.

11
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:19,180
It has hurt every day
since.

12
00:00:19,540 --> 00:00:21,230
Not surgery pain.

13
00:00:21,270 --> 00:00:22,570
I know what that felt
like,

14
00:00:22,570 --> 00:00:23,640
and it went away.

15
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:24,710
This is different.

16
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:25,350
Tight.

17
00:00:25,390 --> 00:00:26,000
Full.

18
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:27,720
Like a band around the
joint

19
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:29,060
that never loosens.

20
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:30,300
And for two years I've

21
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:31,600
been told the same thing.

22
00:00:31,730 --> 00:00:32,630
Give it time.

23
00:00:32,980 --> 00:00:34,430
At six weeks it was
swelling,

24
00:00:34,430 --> 00:00:35,640
and swelling is normal.

25
00:00:36,010 --> 00:00:37,000
At three months,

26
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:38,000
give it six.

27
00:00:38,390 --> 00:00:39,240
At six months,

28
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:40,740
some knees take a full
year.

29
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:41,410
At a year,

30
00:00:41,410 --> 00:00:43,160
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

31
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:44,600
And I didn't just wait.

32
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:46,020
We went down the list.

33
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:47,440
More physical therapy.

34
00:00:47,610 --> 00:00:48,690
Every session,

35
00:00:48,690 --> 00:00:50,240
every exercise at home.

36
00:00:50,510 --> 00:00:51,780
I got stronger.

37
00:00:51,820 --> 00:00:53,140
The tightness never moved.

38
00:00:53,180 --> 00:00:54,930
The pain pills helped,

39
00:00:54,930 --> 00:00:56,090
and that was the problem.

40
00:00:56,260 --> 00:00:58,150
I'm already on enough
every morning,

41
00:00:58,150 --> 00:00:59,170
and nobody could tell me

42
00:00:59,170 --> 00:01:00,380
when I'd get to stop.

43
00:01:00,750 --> 00:01:02,380
Then a nerve block.

44
00:01:02,550 --> 00:01:04,530
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

45
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:05,950
And after that, a second

46
00:01:05,950 --> 00:01:07,200
operation to go back

47
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:08,430
in and do it over.

48
00:01:08,740 --> 00:01:09,970
I said no.

49
00:01:10,350 --> 00:01:12,400
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

50
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:13,590
and my knee felt like

51
00:01:13,590 --> 00:01:15,690
a band was wrapped around
it,

52
00:01:15,690 --> 00:01:18,090
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

53
00:01:18,230 --> 00:01:19,530
Every morning I took
something

54
00:01:19,530 --> 00:01:21,150
for it and went to work.

55
00:01:21,310 --> 00:01:22,630
Couldn't do the stairs,

56
00:01:22,630 --> 00:01:23,710
couldn't stand at the
counter

57
00:01:23,710 --> 00:01:25,210
long enough to finish
dinner,

58
00:01:25,210 --> 00:01:27,180
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

59
00:01:27,180 --> 00:01:29,320
without shifting every two
minutes.

60
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:30,470
At work

61
00:01:30,470 --> 00:01:32,240
I couldn't squat down to a
bottom

62
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:34,180
pallet without grabbing
the rack

63
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:35,260
to get back up.

64
00:01:35,450 --> 00:01:37,010
It woke me at night,

65
00:01:37,010 --> 00:01:39,010
and it turned ordinary
things,

66
00:01:39,010 --> 00:01:40,270
like getting in the car

67
00:01:40,270 --> 00:01:41,360
or up off the couch,

68
00:01:41,360 --> 00:01:42,460
into a decision.

69
00:01:42,660 --> 00:01:43,930
After a long and serious

70
00:01:43,930 --> 00:01:44,850
talk with my wife,

71
00:01:44,850 --> 00:01:46,570
I went back in one more
time.

72
00:01:46,830 --> 00:01:47,960
That was the fourth set

73
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:49,410
of X-rays on this knee.

74
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:51,030
And like the three before
it,

75
00:01:51,030 --> 00:01:53,310
the answer was everything
looks great.

76
00:01:53,370 --> 00:01:54,520
No loosening,

77
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:56,640
no infection, nothing
wrong.

78
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:58,180
Only this time there

79
00:01:58,180 --> 00:01:59,380
was no new number.

80
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:01,800
Nobody said give it
another six months.

81
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:03,520
There was nothing left to
give it.

82
00:02:03,890 --> 00:02:04,880
I sat in the parking

83
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:06,070
lot for a while.

84
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:07,660
Okay, I thought.

85
00:02:07,730 --> 00:02:09,020
Then explain this.

86
00:02:09,150 --> 00:02:11,050
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

87
00:02:11,050 --> 00:02:12,500
I hit my breaking point.

88
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:14,290
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

89
00:02:14,340 --> 00:02:14,830
I had to be

90
00:02:14,830 --> 00:02:16,170
on the dock at six.

91
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:18,150
Everyone in the house was
asleep

92
00:02:18,150 --> 00:02:19,900
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

93
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:20,980
with my leg up,

94
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:23,180
trying to find any angle
where

95
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:25,000
it didn't feel like
something was wrapped

96
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,540
around my knee and
tightening.

97
00:02:26,770 --> 00:02:29,220
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

98
00:02:29,430 --> 00:02:31,020
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

99
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:32,460
And I just thought,

100
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:34,010
is this really my life
now?

101
00:02:34,050 --> 00:02:35,410
I can't live like this.

102
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:36,400
I didn't want my knee

103
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:37,310
to be the thing that made

104
00:02:37,310 --> 00:02:38,910
me quit before I was
ready.

105
00:02:39,060 --> 00:02:40,860
So I made myself a
promise.

106
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:41,910
I wouldn't go a day

107
00:02:41,910 --> 00:02:43,400
without looking for an
answer.

108
00:02:43,590 --> 00:02:44,740
And when I found one,

109
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:45,910
I'd share it with everyone

110
00:02:45,910 --> 00:02:47,230
going through the same
thing.

111
00:02:47,270 --> 00:02:48,900
So I got my laptop

112
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:49,860
out and went looking.

113
00:02:49,900 --> 00:02:51,090
Not for a product.

114
00:02:51,190 --> 00:02:52,340
For an explanation.

115
00:02:52,570 --> 00:02:54,220
Mayo Clinic forums,

116
00:02:54,220 --> 00:02:56,560
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

117
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:57,930
doctor videos,

118
00:02:57,930 --> 00:02:59,370
medical animations.

119
00:02:59,410 --> 00:03:00,700
And that's when I found a
video

120
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:02,390
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

121
00:03:02,430 --> 00:03:03,760
Steven Salinger,

122
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:04,910
whose own wife had been

123
00:03:04,910 --> 00:03:06,360
through exactly this.

124
00:03:06,550 --> 00:03:08,420
But before I say anything
else,

125
00:03:08,420 --> 00:03:09,800
I want to be straight with
you.

126
00:03:10,230 --> 00:03:12,620
You've already had
something work fast.

127
00:03:12,740 --> 00:03:13,480
The ice.

128
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:15,150
The first week of a new
pill.

129
00:03:15,350 --> 00:03:16,770
The good day after a
session.

130
00:03:16,810 --> 00:03:18,030
Then it wore off.

131
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:20,170
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

132
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:22,450
Fast relief isn't relief.

133
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:23,600
It's a preview.

134
00:03:24,150 --> 00:03:25,490
So I'm not going to tell

135
00:03:25,490 --> 00:03:26,920
you this works fast.

136
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:27,950
It doesn't.

137
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:30,610
But if you're willing to
be patient,

138
00:03:30,610 --> 00:03:31,730
and to look at what's
going

139
00:03:31,730 --> 00:03:32,830
on around your new knee

140
00:03:32,830 --> 00:03:34,450
instead of inside it,
there

141
00:03:34,450 --> 00:03:36,620
is a real reason it still
hurts.

142
00:03:37,290 --> 00:03:38,890
And something you can do
about it.

143
00:03:39,230 --> 00:03:40,820
Let me explain what he
said,

144
00:03:40,820 --> 00:03:42,050
because this is what
changed

145
00:03:42,050 --> 00:03:43,160
everything for me.

146
00:03:43,490 --> 00:03:45,270
He started with the
basics.

147
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:46,890
A knee replacement takes
out

148
00:03:46,890 --> 00:03:48,520
the worn joint surfaces

149
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:50,240
and puts in metal and
plastic.

150
00:03:50,390 --> 00:03:52,430
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

151
00:03:52,430 --> 00:03:54,040
you had before the
operation.

152
00:03:54,490 --> 00:03:55,860
That part I already knew.

153
00:03:55,950 --> 00:03:57,430
But then he explained
something

154
00:03:57,430 --> 00:03:58,930
nobody had ever told me.

155
00:03:58,970 --> 00:04:00,150
He said,

156
00:04:00,150 --> 00:04:02,150
think about a swollen foot

157
00:04:02,150 --> 00:04:03,330
inside a shoe.

158
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:05,210
The shoe didn't shrink.

159
00:04:05,350 --> 00:04:06,510
Your foot

160
00:04:06,510 --> 00:04:08,140
is taking up more room,

161
00:04:08,140 --> 00:04:09,760
so everything feels
cramped

162
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:11,300
and tight and squeezed.

163
00:04:11,490 --> 00:04:12,530
Your new knee sits

164
00:04:12,530 --> 00:04:14,060
in a limited space with
living

165
00:04:14,060 --> 00:04:15,930
tissue packed all around
it.

166
00:04:16,150 --> 00:04:18,270
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

167
00:04:18,270 --> 00:04:19,920
had to work through that
tissue.

168
00:04:20,210 --> 00:04:22,550
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

169
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:24,080
At first that's normal.

170
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:25,520
But in some people

171
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:27,050
that swelling can stay
switched

172
00:04:27,050 --> 00:04:28,940
on far longer than
expected.

173
00:04:29,130 --> 00:04:30,910
And swollen tissue takes
up more

174
00:04:30,910 --> 00:04:32,720
room than calm tissue
does.

175
00:04:32,910 --> 00:04:34,300
So when you bend,

176
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:36,140
that tissue gets
compressed.

177
00:04:36,410 --> 00:04:37,370
When you straighten,

178
00:04:37,370 --> 00:04:38,550
it gets pulled tight.

179
00:04:38,590 --> 00:04:39,310
That's the band.

180
00:04:39,350 --> 00:04:41,500
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

181
00:04:41,540 --> 00:04:42,460
And you start being

182
00:04:42,460 --> 00:04:43,650
the one who says,

183
00:04:43,650 --> 00:04:44,540
you go ahead.

184
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:45,570
I'll stay here.

185
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:47,310
And that's exactly why so
much

186
00:04:47,310 --> 00:04:48,930
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

187
00:04:49,020 --> 00:04:50,940
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

188
00:04:50,940 --> 00:04:51,760
around the knee.

189
00:04:52,020 --> 00:04:52,990
Worth doing,

190
00:04:52,990 --> 00:04:54,000
and I'd done it.

191
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:55,500
It does nothing about
tissue

192
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:56,570
taking up room.

193
00:04:56,620 --> 00:04:57,940
A nerve block quiets

194
00:04:57,940 --> 00:04:59,590
the nerve carrying the
signal.

195
00:04:59,810 --> 00:05:01,930
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

196
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:03,850
But when that irritated
tissue

197
00:05:03,850 --> 00:05:05,280
finally calms down,

198
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:06,540
it holds less fluid,

199
00:05:06,540 --> 00:05:08,330
and it takes up less room.

200
00:05:08,550 --> 00:05:09,960
Less room taken up means

201
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:11,890
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

202
00:05:11,950 --> 00:05:13,560
That's what takes the
pressure off.

203
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:15,430
After two years of this,

204
00:05:15,430 --> 00:05:16,870
it finally made sense.

205
00:05:17,370 --> 00:05:19,130
The problem was never the
new knee.

206
00:05:19,170 --> 00:05:21,060
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

207
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:22,960
He calls it the squeeze.

208
00:05:23,070 --> 00:05:25,330
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

209
00:05:25,580 --> 00:05:26,970
I'd bought knee sleeves,

210
00:05:26,970 --> 00:05:28,650
compression braces,

211
00:05:28,650 --> 00:05:30,170
gel insoles,

212
00:05:30,170 --> 00:05:32,770
creams, half of Amazon
really,

213
00:05:32,770 --> 00:05:34,140
and all any of it gave

214
00:05:34,140 --> 00:05:35,330
me was an hour.

215
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:36,710
I even looked at going

216
00:05:36,710 --> 00:05:38,700
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

217
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:40,410
But at $200 a session

218
00:05:40,410 --> 00:05:42,580
with nothing covered by
insurance,

219
00:05:42,580 --> 00:05:43,840
that was a quick no.

220
00:05:43,950 --> 00:05:44,900
Then one night I went

221
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:46,200
back to that knee
replacement

222
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:47,530
group and actually read
it.

223
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:48,880
Thousands of people,

224
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:50,240
years out from surgery,

225
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:53,190
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

226
00:05:53,190 --> 00:05:54,690
nobody could explain.

227
00:05:54,910 --> 00:05:56,750
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

228
00:05:56,750 --> 00:05:58,410
the same thing kept coming
up.

229
00:05:58,670 --> 00:05:59,990
This one device,

230
00:05:59,990 --> 00:06:01,720
and people saying it was
the first

231
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:03,070
thing that made a
difference.

232
00:06:03,260 --> 00:06:05,340
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

233
00:06:05,340 --> 00:06:06,790
alright, here it comes,

234
00:06:06,790 --> 00:06:08,250
he's selling me something,

235
00:06:08,250 --> 00:06:10,460
let me shut that down
right now.

236
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:12,500
I'm only here because I
made myself

237
00:06:12,500 --> 00:06:14,600
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

238
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:15,710
that if I ever found

239
00:06:15,710 --> 00:06:16,980
something that helped,

240
00:06:16,980 --> 00:06:17,990
I'd say so.

241
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:20,130
It's called the KenRelief
Red

242
00:06:20,130 --> 00:06:21,640
Light Therapy Wrap.

243
00:06:22,260 --> 00:06:24,030
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

244
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:25,790
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

245
00:06:25,790 --> 00:06:27,970
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

246
00:06:28,170 --> 00:06:29,840
But I went to their
website anyway,

247
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:30,770
just to see what all

248
00:06:30,770 --> 00:06:31,900
the fuss was about.

249
00:06:32,210 --> 00:06:34,290
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

250
00:06:34,290 --> 00:06:36,160
charge $200 a session for,

251
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:39,030
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

252
00:06:39,030 --> 00:06:39,890
in a wrap you plug

253
00:06:39,890 --> 00:06:41,090
into the wall at home.

254
00:06:41,420 --> 00:06:43,070
Two hundred and forty
lights.

255
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:45,250
Red at 660 nanometers

256
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:47,730
and near-infrared at 850,

257
00:06:47,730 --> 00:06:50,010
run together for the
strongest effect.

258
00:06:50,250 --> 00:06:51,660
Four strength levels.

259
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:53,540
A five to thirty minute
timer.

260
00:06:53,750 --> 00:06:55,170
Then I saw the guarantee.

261
00:06:55,210 --> 00:06:56,340
Ninety days.

262
00:06:56,530 --> 00:06:58,540
Results or your money
back,

263
00:06:58,540 --> 00:07:00,550
no questions, no store
credit,

264
00:07:00,550 --> 00:07:02,630
and you don't even send it
back.

265
00:07:03,020 --> 00:07:05,460
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

266
00:07:05,460 --> 00:07:06,960
days to change my mind.

267
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,150
There wasn't much to lose,

268
00:07:08,150 --> 00:07:09,120
so I ordered it.

269
00:07:09,460 --> 00:07:10,710
Two of them, actually.

270
00:07:10,990 --> 00:07:13,260
Only the right knee was
replaced,

271
00:07:13,260 --> 00:07:15,060
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

272
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:16,820
and I'd done it for two
years.

273
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:19,180
The left one was carrying
the difference.

274
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:20,050
When it came,

275
00:07:20,050 --> 00:07:22,550
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

276
00:07:22,550 --> 00:07:24,070
because I'd been let down
too

277
00:07:24,070 --> 00:07:25,700
many times to get excited.

278
00:07:25,940 --> 00:07:27,500
What I felt was warmth.

279
00:07:27,750 --> 00:07:29,440
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

280
00:07:29,650 --> 00:07:31,140
More like it was coming
from inside

281
00:07:31,140 --> 00:07:32,660
the knee and spreading
around it.

282
00:07:32,940 --> 00:07:33,870
